---
description: "Output format standards for user stories, acceptance criteria, product backlog, work tickets, and effort estimation. Apply when generating or reviewing any of these artifacts."
alwaysApply: true
---

## User Story template

Use this exact template for every user story:

---

### US-[NNN]: [Short descriptive title]

**Type:** [Feature | Enhancement | Technical | Bug]
**Epic:** [Parent epic name]
**Priority:** [Critical | High | Medium | Low]
**Estimate:** [Story points using Fibonacci: 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, 21]

**User Story:**
As a [role], I want to [action] so that [benefit].

**Description:**
[2-3 sentences providing context and business justification.]

**Acceptance Criteria (BDD format):**

- **Scenario 1: [Happy path name]**
  - Given [initial context]
  - When [action performed]
  - Then [expected result]

- **Scenario 2: [Error or edge case name]**
  - Given [initial context]
  - When [action performed]
  - Then [expected result]

- **Scenario 3: [Edge case or alternative flow]**
  - Given [initial context]
  - When [action performed]
  - Then [expected result]

**INVEST Evaluation:**

- Independent: [Yes / No — reason if No]
- Negotiable: [Yes / No — reason if No]
- Valuable: [Yes / No — reason if No]
- Estimable: [Yes / No — reason if No]
- Small: [Yes / No — reason if No]
- Testable: [Yes / No — reason if No]

**Related Stories:** [US-NNN, US-NNN or None]
**Notes:** [Technical notes, constraints, or open questions]

---

## Product Backlog table format

| Priority | ID  | Title | Epic | Business Value | Urgency | Complexity | Risk | Score |
| -------- | --- | ----- | ---- | -------------- | ------- | ---------- | ---- | ----- |

Scoring scale for Business Value, Urgency, Complexity, Risk: 1 (low) to 5 (high).
Score = (Business Value + Urgency) / (Complexity + Risk).
Sort descending by Score.
State the prioritization methodology used and justify the top 3 choices.

## Work Ticket template

Use this exact template for every work ticket:

**Id rule:** Use sequential ids **001, 002, 003, …** per planning pass (`TICKET-001`, not arbitrary bases like 301).

---

### TICKET-[NNN]: [Short descriptive title]

**Parent Story:** US-[NNN]
**Type:** [Feature | Technical Task | Bug | Spike | Test]
**Assignee:** [Team / Role]
**Priority:** [Critical | High | Medium | Low]
**Estimate:** [Fibonacci story points] | [T-shirt size: XS/S/M/L/XL]
**Sprint:** [Sprint number or TBD]
**Labels:** [e.g. backend, frontend, security, database]

**Description:**
[Detailed technical description of what needs to be done and why.]

**Technical Details:**

- [Specific technical requirement or implementation note]
- [API endpoints, data schema changes, or service interactions affected]
- [Non-functional requirements: performance, security, scalability]

**Acceptance Criteria:**

- [ ] [Concrete, verifiable condition 1]
- [ ] [Concrete, verifiable condition 2]
- [ ] [Concrete, verifiable condition 3]

**Dependencies:** [TICKET-NNN or None]
**Related Docs:** [Link to relevant architecture, data model, or design doc]
**Notes:** [Open questions, risks, or additional context]

---

## Effort estimation format

Produce a summary table after all tickets:

| Ticket | Title | Story Points | T-Shirt Size | Confidence | Notes |
| ------ | ----- | ------------ | ------------ | ---------- | ----- |

Confidence scale: High / Medium / Low.
Add a total story points sum at the bottom.
State the estimation methodology used (Fibonacci + T-shirt sizing).
